import json
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(__file__).parent
n=json.loads((p/'review_notes.json').read_text())
def g(ids,kind,why,evidence,repair):
 for i in ids.split():n['graph_decisions'][i]={'classification':kind,'why':why,'evidence':evidence,'repair':repair}
D='Directly optional graph';E='Graph-choice shortcut'
g('PM2D1-LRADJ-EB-002',D,'The stem supplies the below-potential gap and its destination; only falling wages with recovery respects self-correction.','Current intersection relative to LRAS and destination on fixed AD1.','Let the figure establish the gap; compare two plausible wage-adjustment accounts distinguished by their plotted starting and ending equilibria.')
g('PM2D1-LRADJ-L-001',E,'Only the key returns output to potential with a further price increase after a permanent demand increase; rivals deny long-run adjustment.','AD2-AS2 versus AD2-AS1 and LRAS.','Preserve temporary versus permanent effects; offer two coherent long-run accounts with different plotted initial/final price levels.')
g('PM2D1-LRADJ-LB-002',D,'Opposing wage adjustment and a further demand decline are completely specified; the indeterminate net output conclusion needs no image.','Initial recessionary gap and wage-only endpoint; magnitude of the hypothetical further AD decline is not plotted.','Require identifying the plotted wage-only recovery before assessing what the unmeasured new demand shock leaves unresolved; use competing coherent initial-gap readings.')
g('PM2D1-LRADJ-MB-004',D,'Fixed wage contracts alone refute immediate wage-based self-correction; the gap and recovery destination are supplied.','Initial position relative to LRAS and prospective wage-adjustment path.','Let the graph establish the gap and prospective path, then evaluate whether the contract constraint allows that path on the claimed timetable.')
g('PG3-AS-L-001',D,'Temporary bottleneck versus destroyed capacity and the missing information about LRAS are stated verbally; the model-limit answer follows without a plotted reading.','Direction of the AS displacement and absence of an LRAS comparison.','Pair a graph-specific initial short-run effect with the conditional recovery claim; require independent capacity evidence before promising restoration of old potential.')
g('PG3-AS-L-002',D,'The stem supplies both favorable mechanisms and which reverses; partial reversal with persistent productivity gains follows without the graph.','Displayed SRAS displacement, which does not separately identify expectations and productivity contributions.','Require the displayed net shift and then evaluate which part can persist; do not invent a numerical decomposition of the unseparated causes.')
g('PG3-AS-M-002',E,'Only the key is an adverse SRAS shifter; rivals concern AD or movement along a curve.','Direction of AS0 to AS1.','Use genuine favorable and adverse SRAS causes and require matching the actual plotted displacement.')
g('PG3-AS-M-004',D,'The stem calls the production change favorable; only one choice supplies a favorable supply cause.','Direction of AS0 to AS1.','Remove the revealed favorable direction and use plausible opposing supply causes distinguished by the curve displacement.')
g('ECON-SP-ELITE-349',E,'Only the key gives a valid general disinflation lesson; rivals assert permanent unemployment gains or reverse expectations adjustment.','b to d to c: temporary U3 versus long-run U2 at I1.','Offer two coherent disinflation accounts with different labeled short-run/long-run unemployment paths.')
g('ECON-SP-LEGENDARY-9008 ECON-SP-LEGENDARY-9047 ECON-SP-MEDIUMBOSS-3010',E,'Only the key respects how lower expected inflation reconciles disinflation with a return to natural unemployment; competitors deny the expectations mechanism or change the natural rate contrary to the assumptions.','b/d/c and the two short-run curves at I1.','Keep the expectations/credibility inference; provide two economically coherent accounts with different plotted paths or endpoints, plus a correct path with an incorrect expectations explanation.')
g('PM2B3-POL-FB-006',D,'Unreliable enforcement is explicitly the investment constraint; only the key addresses it, regardless of the curve.','Relative marginal gains near A and B.','Require reading which starting position has greater potential gains, then evaluate whether enforcement or machine subsidies permits realizing those gains; keep the institutional constraint.')
g('PM2B3-POL-H-001 PM2B3-POL-LB-001',D,'The stem describes capital deepening/diminishing gains or fixes all productivity determinants; the level-versus-sustained-growth answer follows from that information, while rivals deny diminishing returns.','Concavity and gains over comparable capital increments near A and B.','Require comparison of the plotted capital-deepening gains and evaluate whether extrapolating the earlier growth rate is justified; retain the role of continuing productivity improvements.')
g('ECON-SP-HARD-228',D,'All reference outputs and multiplier/offset inputs are stated; the net $60 billion result identifies the key without reading an intersection.','Y1/Y2/Y3 associations with the AD curves at P.','Keep direct versus multiplied versus already-total offset reasoning, but let the figure supply the destination curve rather than disclosing every output-to-curve association; maintain at least two arithmetically plausible net outcomes.')
g('ECON-SP-HARD-229',E,'AD2 is the only existing AD curve offered; AD4 is not established and SRAS/LRPC are different relationships.','AD3 relative to AD2 and AD1.','Use actual AD positions with plausible degrees of crowding out and require distinguishing partial offset from full reversal.')
g('ECON-SP-LEGENDARY-9024',E,'Only the key is a coherent fiscal AD sequence; other choices invoke unrelated supply or Phillips-curve processes.','AD1 to AD2 to AD3 and the partial return.','Use coherent fiscal sequences with differing direct/induced/offset segments; the depicted path must discriminate which mechanism belongs to each step.')
g('LG-Q-9142',D,'The tax cut, purchases increase and MPC fully determine both impulses and totals; no figure value enters the comparison.','First versus induced horizontal AD segments.','Keep equal stimulus with unequal budget costs; require assigning the calculated direct and induced changes to displayed segments with plausible competing assignments.')
g('PMOE-FX-L-002',E,'Only the key correctly relates appreciation to export competitiveness; rivals reverse relative prices or assert an unsupported equal supply shift.','A-to-B exchange-rate change with fixed price levels.','Retain the offsetting NX channel and movement/shift distinction; offer coherent alternative graph-specific appreciations and their implications.')
g('PMOE-FX-B3-003',D,'Both rates and quantities are disclosed, so all three percentage calculations can be done without the image.','A/B rates and quantities.','Read the initial/final rates from the figure, then interpret reciprocal importer cost changes; avoid adding unrelated arithmetic.')
g('PMOE-FX-L-003',D,'The rightward supply shift and two observationally equivalent causes are stated; the identification limit needs no plotted reading.','Direction of the observed rate/quantity change.','Let the figure supply the joint outcome before assessing which explanations remain consistent and what independent evidence separates them.')
g('PMOE-FX-EL-002',D,'The stem explicitly states both curves shifted right with an unchanged rate; rejecting no demand change and nonidentification of order follow immediately.','Distinct D0/D1 and A/B quantities at the same exchange rate.','Remove the supplied shift/result; require graph evidence to reject the report while retaining the inability to infer temporal order.')
g('PMOE-FX-LB-003',E,'Only the key respects the opposite temporary rate effects and identical final curves; rivals make order permanently change an identical equilibrium or deny intermediate effects.','Intermediate D1/S0 and D0/S1 rates compared with A and B.','Compare two coherent demand-first/supply-first paths using actual intermediate rates; retain path-versus-endpoint reasoning.')
g('PMOE-FX-M-006',D,'Market equilibrium is the intersection of demand and supply by definition; no distinguishing plotted evidence appears in any option.','The actual intersection of D0 and S0.','Use positions from the existing figure and ask why only the intersection clears the market; because the asset has no point labels, use identifiable relative locations without inventing labels or requiring an asset edit.')
g('PMOE-FX-LB-001',E,'Only the key respects NX=NCO given the separately stated net-asset change; rivals either equate gross quantity with NCO or violate the identity.','Unchanged exchange rate and increased gross dollar quantity.','Keep graph evidence separate from net-asset accounting; make two alternatives use the valid identity but differ in the graph-specific exchange-rate/quantity observation.')
g('PMOE-POL-M-003',E,'Given the explicit leftward supply shift, only the key combines appreciation with an admissible quantity response; the other appreciation option increases quantity.','A/B rate change and falling NCO-determined quantity.','Offer two appreciation outcomes with falling quantities and different actual plotted rate changes.')
g('PMOE-POL-B2-001',E,'The stated fall in NCO identifies a leftward vertical supply shift; only one option uses that mechanism.','Positions of S0 and S1 relative to D0.','Preserve the deficit-to-NCO-to-FX chain and compare coherent supply-shift paths whose graph labels/endpoints distinguish the correct case.')
g('ECON-SP-LEGENDARYBOSS-9114',D,'The investment fall, MPC and already-total fiscal offset determine the $60 billion net contraction without either panel.','MS1/MS2 and AD1/AD2 directions and labeled endpoints.','Keep linked monetary/fiscal transmission and double-counting diagnosis, but require matching the computed offset to the direction and labeled path actually shown.')
g('ECON-SP-FINALBOSS-4006 ECON-SP-LEGENDARYBOSS-9103',E,'Only the key respects unchanged productive capacity and wage/expectations adjustment; all rivals shift potential or reverse the adjustment mechanism.','Initial output above LRAS, AS2-to-AS1 adjustment and final Y1.','Keep temporary demand gains versus capacity and expectations reasoning; use competing coherent accounts with different plotted endpoints, including a correct endpoint paired with a wrong mechanism.')
g('ECON-SP-LEGENDARYBOSS-9102 ECON-SP-LEGENDARYBOSS-9104',E,'Only the key permits demand support to restore output without undoing the adverse supply effect, or separates demand support from lower-cost self-correction; rivals deny the basic price/output mechanism.','Y3/P2 compared with Y1/P1 and Y1/P3.','Keep the policy counterfactual; provide two economically coherent comparisons with different graph-specific starting/final intersections rather than impossible price reversals.')
g('ECON-SP-FINALBOSS-4010 ECON-SP-LEGENDARYBOSS-9107',E,'Only the key respects expectations adjustment and the need for renewed inflation surprises to hold unemployment below natural; rivals shift the natural rate or reverse expectations effects.','c/a/b and U1 versus U2, I1 versus I2.','Preserve the dynamic policy tradeoff; distinguish coherent labeled paths and then test whether the proposed fixed inflation can sustain the depicted unemployment.')
g('ECON-SP-FINALBOSS-4012 ECON-SP-FINALBOSS-4013 ECON-SP-LEGENDARYBOSS-9108',E,'Only the key respects temporary disinflation costs and eventual expectations adjustment with unchanged natural unemployment; rival mechanisms contradict the stated assumptions.','b/d/c and U3/U2 along fixed I1.','Retain credibility, contract timing and short/long-run comparison; use two plausible endpoint/path accounts that require reading which curve and unemployment level the figure assigns.')
g('ECON-SP-LEGENDARYBOSS-9115',E,'Only the key recognizes that increased money demand plus money supply has opposing rate pressures whereas increased demand plus decreased supply reinforces them; all rivals deny these mechanisms.','e-to-d and g-to-a actual rate changes.','Require comparing the plotted net rates as well as identifying opposing versus reinforcing mechanisms; offer two valid mechanism descriptions with different plotted net outcomes.')
g('ECON-SP-LEGENDARYBOSS-9109',E,'Only the key distinguishes weaker-demand movement from a changed short-run Phillips relation; every rival denies the movement/shift distinction.','b/c/f inflation and unemployment positions on SRPC1/SRPC2.','Use competing valid demand-versus-shift explanations with different labeled paths; include a correct path with a mistaken expectations inference.')
